6578 1071 "Consider the function\n$f(x) = \\mathbf{1}[x \\geq 1] \\cdot x^2 + \\mathbf{1}[x < 1] \\cdot (-x)$.\nWhat is $f(-2)$?" 13194139535595 17592186045417 false] [17592186166578 1074 "The indicator function $\\mathbf{1}[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n![](images/66/6698e70e8d5cc4c4e4fd3578170ed7e43a2a907e2ab0397352882d87af2d32e1.svg)\n\nFor $x = -2,$ we evaluate each indicator function:\n\n- $\\mathbf{1}[x \\geq 1] = \\mathbf{1}[-2 \\geq 1] = 0$ (since $-2 \\geq 1$ is false)\n\n- $\\mathbf{1}[x < 1] = \\mathbf{1}[-2 < 1] = 1$ (since $-2 < 1$ is true)\n\nSubstituting into the expression for $f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =1[-2\\ge 1]\\cdot (-2)^{2}+1[-2<1]\\cdot (-(-2)) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the indicator functions act as a \"switch\": since $x = -2 < 1,$ the first term vanishes and only the second term contributes to the result." 13194139535595 17592186045417 true] [17592186166578 1074 "The indicator function $\\mathbf{1}[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n${1,\\begin{vmatrix}if [math]P[/math] is true, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}if [math]P[/math] is false$.\n\nFor $x = -2$, we evaluate each indicator function:\n\n- $\\mathbf{1}[x \\geq 1] = \\mathbf{1}[-2 \\geq 1] = 0$ (since $-2 \\geq 1$ is false)\n- $\\mathbf{1}[x < 1] = \\mathbf{1}[-2 < 1] = 1$ (since $-2 < 1$ is true)\n\nSubstituting into the expression for $f(x)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-2) &= 1[- 2 \\ge 1] \\cdot (-2)^{2} + 1[- 2 < 1] \\cdot (- (-2)) \\\\\n&= 0 \\cdot 4 + 1 \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the indicator functions act as a \"switch\": since $x = -2 < 1$, the first term vanishes and only the second term contributes to the result." 13194139535595 17592186045417 false] [17592186166579 1071 "Let $H = \\{-5, -3, -1, 1\\}$. Which of the following is equivalent to $\\mathbf{1}_H(0)$?\n\n1. $\\mathbf{1}[0 \\in \\{-5, -3, -1, 1\\}]$\n2. $